      // character only, so anything starting with a digit was accepted whole
      // and handed to parseInt. "1,000" and "1e3" both became 1 and "3.5"
      // became 3, all with bad = false, so no check fired — and because a
      // usable row switches the diagram to per-covariate mode, the shared
      // 365-day look-back was suppressed as well. Someone asking for a
      // 1000-day baseline window got a protocol asserting a one-day one, and
      // nothing on screen said otherwise. Require the whole field to be a
      // whole number of days, optionally with the word "days" after it.
